course: dictionary
lesson: 9669
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word subway is a good example. «Under big cities, electric trains run in tunnels called the Underground, the Tube, the metro or the subway.» Electric trains in tunnels under a city means the subway is an underground railway.
explain: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a subway means something different: a path or tunnel under a busy road, for people to walk through. Clues like road, cross and walk tell you which meaning fits. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Word parts can help too. Sub- means under, as in submarine and subway. Pre- means before, as in preview and prehistoric. If you know sub- means under, you can guess that a subway is something under the ground or under a road.
fact: Subway means an underground railway in a city, in the USA and Canada.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia, a subway is a path or tunnel under a road for people to walk through.
fact: Sub- means under, so a subway is a way under something.
fact: Other names for underground city trains include the Underground, the Tube and the metro.
fact: Check the meaning by reading the words around the word: do they talk about trains, or about walking under a road?
exercise: «A girl in Toronto stood too close to the edge of a subway platform.» In this sentence, what is a platform? | *The raised place at a station where you wait for a train | A path under a road | A tunnel for walking through | A ticket office
exercise: «Under big cities, electric trains run in tunnels called the Underground, the Tube, the metro or the subway.» What is a subway here? | A bridge over a river | A bus lane | *An underground railway | A path under a busy road
exercise: In the UK, what is a subway used for? | Swimming across a river | *Crossing a busy road safely on foot | Flying over the city | Parking cars
test: In the USA and Canada, what is a subway? | *An underground railway in a city | A bus station | A path under a road for walkers | A tall bridge over a river
test: Sub- means what? | Over | *Under | Around | Before
exam: Read this: «pre- means before (preview, prehistoric); sub- means under (submarine, subway).» What does the sub- in subway mean? | *Under | Before | Inside | Over
